            <ArticleTitle>Removal of total prostheses of the hip. Review of twenty six cases.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>57-67</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The &quot;painful prosthesis&quot; is a difficult problem. Removal is often the best solution. Out of 566 McKee-Farrar prostheses, twenty six (4.2 per cent) were removed. The causes that made removal advisable are analysed. The methods used and the results obtained are described.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
